{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310835,"nonce":"N8MmqeUDVq7FZGjjcw49osLL5qs=","title":"Haxification of nue — Phase 3 DONE: pure-Haxe Q4_K_M×Q8_K dot kernel runs bit-exact NATIVE + WASM (test_q4km_dot.hx, 32586379). Landed: ...","message":"Mission: move nue's quant-matmul dot off Rust FFI into pure Haxe for superior **wasm** decode latency (native already at NEON-SDOT parity; the win is removing the FFI fusion barrier — the #1 wasm lever). Plan: [[perf_wasm_v8_vs_wasmtime_2x]], docs/plans/haxe-quant-matmul-vectordot.md. Phases 0-2 (element-aware wasm int vectors, SIMD4i32/SIMD16i8, VectorDot→SDOT all backends) were already DONE. This is Phase 3 (port the Q4_K_M×Q8_K dot to Haxe) prerequisites.\n\n\n1. **8a007a39 — SIMD16i8 lane-wise bitwise + shift** (the #1 gap: Q4 nibble unpack). Added static `SIMD16i8.and/or/xor` (vector⊕vector) + `shl/shr/ushr` (vector-by-scalar i32 amount) as systems.rs MIR wrappers over `vector_bin_op`; runtime_mapping `rayzor_SIMD16i8` entries; SIMD16i8.hx externs. wasm already lowered these; the gap was **native Cranelift had NO vector shift** (Shl/Shr/Ushr → Unsupported-op Err) — added `ishl`/`sshr|ushr`(Shr picks by elem signedness)/`ushr` in cranelift_backend VectorBinOp arm. STATIC methods (instance dispatch on i8x16 mis-routes to SIMD4f — simd_vector_class has no i8x16 arm). Gate: test_simd16i8_bitops.hx via proven dot+sum read-out (and=112 ushr=160 shr=-96 shl=1792 or=112 xor=96), bit-identical N+W.\n2. **d3c3bb1e — SIMD coreType abstracts keep vector type as fn params.** A SIMD4f/4i32/16i8 passed as a fn param was typed I64 (silent 128→64-bit truncation; crashed in codegen: swiden_low \"invalid type for merge_lanes\" / aarch64 emit assert). convert_type's coreType-abstract branch matched the SIMD vector types only via native_name, which is absent for a param symbol → fell to is_systems_type (SIMD* are mir_wrapper classes) → I64. FIX (hir_to_mir convert_type ~21854): detect via native_name OR qualified_name OR bare name, before is_systems_type. Unblocks helper-fn decomposition of SIMD kernels.\n\nThe Phase 3 payoff landed. compiler/tests/haxe/test_q4km_dot.hx PASSES native AND wasm.\n3. ✅ **Bytes→Ptr load path** (2230417a + wasm wiring 32586379). `Bytes.address():Usize` → HaxeBytes data ptr. `SIMD16i8.load(Ptr.fromRaw(buf.address() + Usize.fromInt(off)))`. **CORRECTION: Bytes ARE guest-resident on wasm** (write_haxe_bytes_in_wasm host_alloc's header+data in guest linear mem — the earlier \"host-side\" claim was WRONG). The wasm test only failed because haxe_bytes_data_address wasn't registered in the wasm_runner; added a host closure returning the guest data offset via read_haxe_bytes_header. Now load works in-guest. (Native haxe_bytes_data_address = HaxeBytes.ptr.)\n4. ✅ **f16→f32 decode** (in test_q4km_dot, exact). GOTCHA: `:Int` on every bitwise-derived intermediate ([[bugs_inferred_int_bitwise_float_div]]).\n5. ✅ **The kernel** = test_q4km_dot.hx q4Dot/subDot: 8 sub-blocks, q4_k_get_scale_min unpack, nibble unpack (AND 0x0F / USHR 4 via SIMD16i8), 2×SIMD4i32.dot per 32-elem sub-block → sum (exact int sdot), f32 fold `d·sc6·sdot − dmin·mn6·bsum32`, ×x.d. Oracle = vec_dot_q4_K_q8_K_scalar (q4_k_m.rs:233). f64-vs-f32 fold → ~f32 precision (tol 0.01), int dot exact. Dot's `b` operand must be i7 (−64..63): Q4 nibbles 0..15 = `a`, activation i8 = `b` (keep activations in range).\n6. ✅ **Bit-exact gate** = golden_gate test (q4_k_m.rs #[cfg(test)] mod, run `cargo test -p rayzor-runtime-core --release golden_q4_dot_for_haxe_gate -- --nocapture`): 2 pinned blocks, case1=75.8399963379, case2=-14.1860599518 (varied scales/per-lane nibbles/negative acts). Haxe matches both N+W.\n\ntest_q4km_qmatmul.hx: a full pure-Haxe Q4_K_M qmatmul matches Rust QTensor.matmulXTQ on a REAL Q4_K_M QTensor, native AND in-guest wasm (maxRelErr 7e-8 / 0 — f32 precision). Landed this session:\n- **QTensor.dataPtr():Usize** (0ccb20d0) — weight base ptr, all 6 layers + wasm side-module rebuilt (cargo build --release --target wasm32-wasip1-threads in runtime-wasm).\n- **SIMD16i8.get(lane)** (54747348) — in-guest byte extract for the block header (d/dmin/scales); Ptr\u003cInt\u003e.deref SEGFAULTS (use this); normalized signed via (r\u003c\u003c24)\u003e\u003e24.\n- Haxe Q8_K activation quant (absmax/round-away/bsums) matches the runtime quantizer to f32 precision.\n- QTensor build for tests: fromBytesQ4KM(bytes, rows, cols) (haxe.io.Bytes == rayzor.Bytes). NOTE: **fromFloat32 IGNORES its QScheme arg — always makes INT8** (maps to rayzor_qtensor_from_f32_int8); matmulXTQ rejects INT8 → empty result. Use fromBytesQ4KM for Q4_K_M.\n- 3 wasm/compiler bugs hit + worked around: [[bugs_empty_array_literal_float_inference]] (untyped `var a=[]` → Array\u003cInt\u003e, truncates floats; annotate), [[bugs_wasm_inline_if_reassign_nested_loop]] (`if(c)v=k;` in nested loop fails wasm compile; use ternary), Ptr\u003cInt\u003e.deref segfault.\n\nREMAINING Phase 4: (a) lift the kernel into a reusable location + own the row/band loop via WorkerPool.parallelRows (verify nue.Linear import cascade gone); (b) wire nue.Linear.forward to use it; (c) **the throughput A/B** (Haxe qmatmul vs qt.matmulXTQ, wasm decode tok/s — the first meaningful perf number; isolated dot bench is low-signal, native is saturated, the win needs FFI-fusion which only shows fused) + France→Paris greedy. Q8_K quant can stay Rust (once/matmul) or use the Haxe port.\n\nSeam: replace the per-block Rust dot in the qmatmul band loop with this Haxe dot.\nSTART HERE — concrete next steps:\n1. **Expose the QTensor weight data pointer to Haxe.** QTensor.hx TODAY has NO data accessor — only qtensor_rows/cols/numel/scheme/dequant/matmul*/free (compiler/haxe-std/rayzor/ds/QTensor.hx). Add one mirroring `Tensor.data():Ptr\u003cFloat\u003e` (@:native tensor_data, Tensor.hx:434): a `qtensor_data_ptr` runtime extern returning RayzorQTensor.data (struct @ runtime/src/quant.rs:126) as Usize. Guest-resident on wasm (same as Bytes — proven this session).\n2. **Weight block addressing** (from quant.rs:731-735): blocks_per_row = qt.cols / 256 (Q4_K_M); row r block b is at `qt.data + (r*blocks_per_row + b)*144`. So the Haxe kernel loops n in 0..rows, b in 0..blocks_per_row, dots block bytes (via SIMD16i8.load on that guest ptr) against the Q8_K activation block b, sums → y[n].\n3. **Q8_K activation**: keep Rust quant (once/matmul, NEON, bit-identical) — expose its scratch ptr (X_Q8K_SCRATCH / prepare_x_q8k_blocks_into, quant.rs:1052) to Haxe, OR port quantize_block_q8_K to Haxe (q8_k.rs:174: absmax, d=absmax/127, round-half-away, 16-wide bsums). For Q8K the Haxe kernel needs qs[i8;256]+bsums[i16;16]+d per block.\n4. **Drive the row/band loop in Haxe** via WorkerPool.parallelRows (matmulXTQChunk path) — RE-VERIFY the old nue.Linear import cascade is gone (likely, post WorkerPool fix chain, e1124335). Per-block FFI crossing (~65k/matmul) is why the row loop must be Haxe too (not a per-block FFI).\n5. **Gate**: a small Haxe qmatmul vs qt.matmulXTQ(x) on a constructed QTensor (qtensor_from_float32 or from_bytes_q4_k_m) → equal y. Then wire nue.Linear.forward → France→Paris greedy match + decode tok/s A/B vs FFI (model ~/.cache/huggingface/.../Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf; pkill -9 hygiene; bit-exact/coherent BEFORE perf claim).\nKEY de-risk from this session: QTensor weight data is guest-resident on wasm (like Bytes), and Tensor.data() proves guest pointers reach Haxe — so NO host/guest bridging problem for the weights. The kernel itself (test_q4km_dot.hx q4Dot) is ready to lift into a reusable location (nue/ or rayzor.ds) when wiring.\n\nSeam is CLEAN at the Rust layer: the band loop already calls a per-block `vec_dot_q4_K_q8_K(\u0026Q4KMBlock,\u0026Q8KBlock)-\u003ef32` (quant.rs:1841). BUT nothing (weight ptr, Q8KBlock, the dot) is exposed to Haxe, AND a per-block FFI crossing means ~65k crossings/matmul → likely need the ROW LOOP in Haxe too. The band loop+threading are Rust (worker_pool.parallel_rows); a Haxe band loop uses **WorkerPool.parallelRows** (rayzor.concurrent.WorkerPool — NumaPool was RENAMED to WorkerPool; the old `NumaPool` name is gone, all source comments updated this session). WorkerPool.parallelRows exists + works end-to-end ([[project_workerpool_fix_chain]]); the old \"importing it from nue.Linear traps\" claim PREDATES that fix chain → likely already unblocked, RE-VERIFY (don't assume the matmulXTQChunk/WorkerPool route is still blocked). Q8_K activation quant stays Rust (once/matmul, NEON, bit-identical) and only its scratch ptr is exposed. Self-hosting (not latency) is the justification on native; the wasm latency win is the real target.\n\n- Build: `cargo build --release --features llvm-backend -p rayzor --bin rayzor` (NOT -p compiler). Run: `./target/release/rayzor run f.hx [--wasm] --no-cache`. wasm output truncated by `[wasm-linker]` logs — grep PASS/FAIL.\n- relaxed_dot is bit-identical only when the i7x16 operand (dot's `b`) is −64..63; Q4 nibbles 0..15 and the read-out splat(1) satisfy it. a (first operand) can be full i8.\n- Full suite (./run_haxe_tests.sh) flaky failures = test_copy / test_copy_clone_identity exit-133 (W0020), NOT regressions — never attribute without N≥40 A/B.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_haxe_q4_dot_phase3` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}